{"diagnosis": "Failing signal is mem_la_addr with low bits 2'b10 vs expected 2'b00, causing TRAP: fetch misalign addr low bits nonzero. Line 382 hardcodes {..,2'b10} for both fetch and data addresses so every access is misaligned by 2 bytes. This directly explains FAIL 0xdead on aligned NOP fetch.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -382,1 +382,1 @@
-	assign mem_la_addr = (mem_do_prefetch || mem_do_rinst) ? {next_pc[31:2] + mem_la_firstword_xfer, 2'b10} : {reg_op1[31:2], 2'b10};
+	assign mem_la_addr = (mem_do_prefetch || mem_do_rinst) ? {next_pc[31:2] + mem_la_firstword_xfer, 2'b00} : {reg_op1[31:2], 2'b00};", "expected": "tohost PASS (FAIL 0xdead cleared, no fetch misalign trap)"}

